\subsection{Substantive Effects}

Given the high number of observations available in this data set, there is likely 
sufficient power to detect effects that are substantively quite small yet remain 
statistically significant. In order to better understand this, I use simulations 
to illustrate the substantive impact of several of the key variables identified 
in the models above on school board contestation.  

\subsubsection{Fixed Effects}

The tables above provide the coefficients and standard errors for the models, but 
logistic regression coefficients can be difficult to interpret -- especially on 
data that has been rescaled. In order to better demonstrate the impact of key 
variables, I provide simulations from the models above that show the impact on the 
probability of contestation conditional on changes in those variables. 

<<fixefplot1, eval=TRUE, fig.cap="Coefficient Plot for Full Model Fixed Effects",fig.height=8.5, fig.width=8>>=
sim1 <- FEsim(fullmodMMCon, nsims = 1000); sim1$dv <- "Contest"
sim2 <- FEsim(fullmodMMni, nsims = 1000); sim2$dv <- "No Incumb."
sim3 <- FEsim(fullmodMMd, nsims = 1000); sim3$dv <- "Defeat"


simPlot <- do.call(rbind, list(sim1, sim2, sim3))
simPlot$dv <- factor(simPlot$dv, levels = c("No Incumb.", "Contest", "Defeat"))
alpha <- 1.96
simPlot$upr <- simPlot$meanEff + (alpha*simPlot$sdEff)
simPlot$lwr <- simPlot$meanEff - (alpha*simPlot$sdEff)

simPlot$color <- "Not Sig."
simPlot$color <- ifelse(simPlot$lwr >0 | simPlot$upr < 0, "Sig", "Not Sig.")

ggplot(simPlot, aes(x = variable, y = meanEff, ymax = upr, 
                    ymin = lwr, color = color)) + 
  scale_color_brewer(palette = "Dark2") + 
  geom_point() + geom_errorbar(h=1.5) +
  geom_hline(yintercept = 0, size = I(1.1), color = I("black"), linetype = 2, 
             alpha = I(0.6)) +
  coord_flip() + 
  facet_wrap(~dv) + 
  theme_dpi(base_size=12) +theme(legend.position = "bottom") + 
  labs(x = "Variable", y = "Effect", color = "Stat. Sig.")

# confint(fullmodMMni, method = "Wald", level = 0.9)
@

<<fixefSub1, fig.cap="Substantive Effect on Contestation Across Cases">>=
seplotdf <- substEffSimFE(fullmodMMCon, "schoolMillShare", ncases = 12L, 
                          unscale = moddatScale, re = TRUE)

ggplot(seplotdf, aes(x = newvarUnscale, y = yhat)) +
  geom_line(aes(group = caseID)) + 
    geom_ribbon(aes(ymin=lwr, ymax=upr, group = caseID),
                     alpha=0.4) + 
  facet_wrap(~caseID) + 
  geom_rug(data = dist_turn, aes(x = schoolMillShare, y = NULL)) + 
  theme_dpi(base_size=12) + 
  labs(x = "School Millrate Share", y = "Pr(Contested)")

@


\subsubsection{District and Year Variation}

By far the most variation is explained both by year effects across districts and 
by district effects across years. These effects represent the sum of unobserved 
characteristics that do not vary within districts over time, and of characteristics 
that vary over time across all districts. 

Across year effects.
<<fixefSubYear, fig.cap="Substantive Effect on Contestation for Years">>=
seplotdf <- substEffSimFE(fullmodMMni, "year", ncases = 4L, re = TRUE, alpha = 0.1)

p1 <- ggplot(seplotdf, aes(x = year, y = yhat)) +
  geom_line(aes(group = caseID)) + 
    geom_ribbon(aes(ymin=lwr, ymax=upr, group = caseID),
                     alpha=0.4) + 
  geom_hline(yintercept = quantile(fitted(fullmodMMni), prob = 0.25)) + 
  geom_hline(yintercept = quantile(fitted(fullmodMMni), prob = 0.75)) + 
  facet_wrap(~caseID, nrow=1) +
  theme_dpi(base_size=12) + 
  theme(strip.text = element_blank(), strip.background = element_blank()) +  
  labs(x = "Year", y = "Pr(Non-Incumbent)", title= "Year Effect Across Observations")


seplotdf <- substEffSimFE(fullmodMMCon, "year", ncases = 4L, re = TRUE, alpha = 0.1)

p2 <- ggplot(seplotdf, aes(x = year, y = yhat)) +
  geom_line(aes(group = caseID)) + 
    geom_ribbon(aes(ymin=lwr, ymax=upr, group = caseID),
                     alpha=0.4) + 
  geom_hline(yintercept = quantile(fitted(fullmodMMni), prob = 0.25)) + 
  geom_hline(yintercept = quantile(fitted(fullmodMMni), prob = 0.75)) + 
  facet_wrap(~caseID, nrow=1) +
  theme_dpi(base_size=12) + 
  theme(strip.text = element_blank(), strip.background = element_blank()) +  
  labs(x = "Year", y = "Pr(Contested)", title= "Year Effect Across Observations")


seplotdf <- substEffSimFE(fullmodMMd, "year", ncases = 4L, re = TRUE, alpha = 0.1)

p3 <- ggplot(seplotdf, aes(x = year, y = yhat)) +
  geom_line(aes(group = caseID)) + 
    geom_ribbon(aes(ymin=lwr, ymax=upr, group = caseID),
                     alpha=0.4) + 
  geom_hline(yintercept = quantile(fitted(fullmodMMni), prob = 0.25)) + 
  geom_hline(yintercept = quantile(fitted(fullmodMMni), prob = 0.75)) + 
